  body: |
    # Continental shelf prescribed employment in the source

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source describes a continental shelf worker by prescribed employment and says the relevant employment can be under a contract of service or otherwise in an appointed or designated area.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 078080–078081 are qualified by the separate accident and disease definitions at 078084. No ordinary land-based employment or whole-UK territorial rule is substituted.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 078080, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a7f779940f0b6230268fabd/dmgch0707.pdf#page=7)
    - [DMG 078081, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a7f779940f0b6230268fabd/dmgch0707.pdf#page=7)
    - [DMG 078084, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a7f779940f0b6230268fabd/dmgch0707.pdf#page=7)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is a model-assisted, unreviewed interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP source. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. No specialist acceptance, current-law reconciliation or complete coverage of this chapter part is claimed. References to EU law, countries and benefits retain the scope and date context of the cited text; they do not establish applicability to a person or a later regime. Machine extraction may alter reading order and characters; no visual PDF review is claimed.

